WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:05.670 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  archbishop emeritus desmond tutu asked  for a simple ceremony  a low-key funeral for a plain-spoken man  and the nation did its best  [Music]  the arch as he was known was carried in  a simple coffin as the cathedral choir  sang a hymn  but there was no honor guard on display  nor great flowery bouquets  and there were just a hundred in  attendance due to covert rules  but tutu is the object of limitless  affection  and his daughter naomi gave her thanks  because we shared him with the world  you shared part of the love you held for  him  with us  we say  thank you  daddy  for the many ways you showed us love  for the many times  you challenged us  for the many times  you comforted us  the south african government called it a  category one funeral a solemn event of  remembrance  but as the president began the eulogy he  told the country to cheer itself up  that's what tutu would have wanted  if  arch  bishop desmond duty were here  he would have said hey  hey why are you looking so glam  so unhappy  he would have wanted to elicit a smile  and laughter  from amongst all of us  that was the type of person that he was  but tutu also led the fight against  white minority rule in the 1980s and  played a pivotal role in the creation of  a new rainbow nation  helping us to come to terms with the  past  was among the most arduous tasks  of our new nation  and archbishop desmond tutu  played a seminal role in this whole  process  while our beloved madiba was the father  of our democracy  archbishop desmond tutu  was the spiritual father  of our new nation we will be free  appointed archbishop of cape town in  1986 desmond tutu took on the  politicians and police of the apartheid  regime  and he remained an uncomfortable  opponent for the country's leaders in  the democratic era  tutu spoke truth to power wherever he  found it and he was given the nobel  peace prize for his efforts  he never ceased to speak prophetically  he never ceased to speak powerfully he  never ceased to shed light  many nobel prize winners like fades with  time his group writer  his simple coffin made from the cheapest  pine was carried from the cathedral by  the leaders of the church before his  body was taken for an environmentally  friendly cremation  a modest man desmond tutu has left an  extraordinary legacy  john sparks sky news

